## FILE COMPLETENESS VERIFICATION (Non-Negotiable)
After writing any .test.ts file and BEFORE running vitest, verify the file is 
syntactically complete by running: node --check <file>. A file that passes tsc 
--noEmit but fails vitest with "unexpected EOF" or "unexpected token" was written 
truncated — tsc can sometimes accept partial files while esbuild/acorn cannot.
The required workflow: (1) Write the test file. (2) Run: node --check <file> — 
if non-zero, add the missing closing brackets/braces. (3) Only then run vitest.
Truncation: grep -c \"{\" <file> and grep -c \"}\" <file> must be equal.

## ASYNC SERVER TEARDOWN (Non-Negotiable for all server tests)
Any test file that creates, imports, or starts a server instance MUST include 
afterAll cleanup: afterAll(async () => { await server.close() }). Port 0 lets 
the OS assign a free port (prevents EADDRINUSE). Pattern:
afterAll: await new Promise((resolve, reject) => { server.close((err) => 
  err ? reject(err) : resolve(undefined)) }).

## EXIT CODE SUBPROCESS ASSERTION (Non-Negotiable for CLI tests)
When testing CLI entry points, assert result.status explicitly via spawnSync.
result.status === 0 (success), 1 (logic error), 2 (arg-parse failure).
Asserting only stdout without result.status misses the actual AC.
